From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: offload CT wireless IPv6 routed flows

Enable untagged TCP/UDP IPv6 five-tuple routing through CT PPE and WED.
Retain software forwarding for NAT66, encapsulated and non-unicast flows.
Accept CT IPv6 only from netfilter flowtable. Keep separate FT and flower
callbacks so ordinary flower IPv6 rules stay in software, including fixed
TOS matches that the five-tuple hardware cannot express. Retain IPv4 and
non-CT callback behavior. Validate IPv6 keys and masks at the shared PPE
callback, rejecting TTL, unsupported TCP flags and extra matches.
Use immutable source-MAC slots owned by CT for IPv6 entries. Poll write
completion, quarantine failed slots, and zero owned words only after both
PPE SRAM banks have drained and quiesced. Serialize the update window
with native GDM MAC updates. Avoid UPDMEM reads: CT returns the last
DATA write instead of the addressed table word.

Extend the short-frame IFC guard to IPv6 payload lengths 0..17, preserving
separate IPv4 and IPv6 rule state and retryable rollback. Decode the proper
IPv4 or IPv6 egress layout when flushing stations, and include packet type
in tuple matching to avoid invalidating a reused row of another type.

